# ClawPilot Heartbeat Checklist

## Purpose

The heartbeat is a minimal, periodic self-check to ensure:
- Urgent tasks are surfaced promptly
- No stale blockers go unnoticed
- System remains responsive and on-track

## Heartbeat Frequency

- Standard: Every 4 hours during workday (Asia/Singapore time)
- Extended: Every 6 hours during off-hours
- On-Demand: When Mira requests status

## Checklist

### 1. Urgent Tasks Scan
- [ ] Check for tasks marked urgent or high-priority
- [ ] Verify no urgent items are past deadline
- [ ] Flag any time-sensitive matters requiring immediate attention

### 2. Blocker Status
- [ ] Review active blockers list
- [ ] Confirm no blockers have been stale >24 hours
- [ ] Identify any new blockers since last heartbeat

### 3. Channel Health
- [ ] Telegram: Check for unread mentions
- [ ] Discord: Check for unread mentions
- [ ] No critical messages missed

### 4. Memory Integrity
- [ ] MEMORY.md is current
- [ ] Daily log exists for today
- [ ] No corruption or missing data

### 5. Confirmation Queue
- [ ] Review pending drafts awaiting Mira's approval
- [ ] Flag any drafts that may have expired
- [ ] Prioritize time-sensitive confirmations

## Heartbeat Output Format

[HEARTBEAT] YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM SGT
+-- Urgent Tasks: X found (Y past deadline)
+-- Blockers: X active (Y stale >24h)
+-- Channels: Telegram [OK], Discord [OK]
+-- Memory: [OK]
+-- Pending Confirmations: X items

## Escalation Rules

Condition                          | Action
----------------------------------|-------------------------------
Urgent task past deadline          | Immediate alert to Mira
Blocker stale >48h                 | Flag for review
Channel unread backlog >10         | Summary provided
Pending confirmation >24h          | Gentle reminder

## Notes

- Heartbeat is silent if all checks pass
- Only reports when action may be needed
- Never auto-sends; always drafts for confirmation

